Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:09.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  personal achievement sponsored by Stover  school ian leslie ian is represented  Sheldon Bowling Club for 20 years  joining the team when he was just 10  years old ian has enjoyed great success  locally regionally and nationally and he  also represents Devon in England a  long-standing member of his local club  last season Ian played his part in  helping win the Mid Devon League and the  county team trophy and in July ian was  honored to be selected to join the  England squad in the recent home  international series at Royal lemmings  in Spa bowling against Wales Ireland and  Scotland and finishing in a very close  second place the same month ian was also  selected as one of four men to play  against Australia in a one-off Test  match Mollie Mayhew Molly has congenital  proximal radioulnar synostosis which can  prove physically challenging for her  this does not stop her from trying her  best  she gives every dance lesson and every  BMX session 110 percent resulting in her  achieving a silver medal in BMX and a  gold medal in dance events at the Youth  Games after having anxiety issues during  competing in the Youth Games Molly  overcame fears of taking on some of the  larger features of the skate park to get  awarded a silver medal with their  teammates this is given Molly so much  confidence and encouraged her to thrive  not just at bmxing but with her dancing  to Molly's efforts at the Youth Games  help team bridge get overall 1st place  at Doris in July  [Music]

